# CDARS line-ending policy.
#
# Line endings are a property of this repository, not of each developer's Git
# installation. Without this file the outcome depends on core.autocrlf, which
# the Git for Windows installer sets to `true` at SYSTEM level -- that is what
# rewrote 318 working-tree files to CRLF after a branch checkout and broke 35
# backend and 2 frontend tests that assert on LF-delimited source text.

# Default: Git detects text vs binary per file. Every file detected as text is
# stored LF in the repository and checked out LF on every platform, overriding
# core.autocrlf and core.eol. Detected binaries are left untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts stay LF. backend/docker/entrypoint.sh is the container
# entrypoint and a CRLF shebang fails to execute on Linux.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows launchers keep CRLF -- cmd.exe can mis-parse LF-only batch files.
# Composer generates one .bat per vendor binary (8 are tracked under
# backend/vendor/bin). No .cmd is tracked today, but Composer and npm emit them.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Images and Windows executables: never convert, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.exe binary
